1
00:00:00,911 --> 00:00:09,305
Welcome to the Europe capitals, episode six of six. First, I clear the chosen
names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:09,958 --> 00:00:20,790
Four capitals close the series: the two of the Iberian peninsula, the old
capital of the Mediterranean, and the smallest of the island capitals.

3
00:00:21,448 --> 00:00:23,956
Let's bring Madrid into view.

4
00:00:27,425 --> 00:00:35,482
Madrid stands on the Manzanares river in the centre of Spain, on a plateau
about 650 metres above the sea.

5
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:44,116
From Arabic al-Majrit, "source of water": the Moorish fortress was named for
its streams, and the Christians kept the name.

6
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:54,974
Remember Madrid as the source of water and the highest capital in Europe at
650 metres, with the Prado holding Spain's finest painting.

7
00:00:55,661 --> 00:00:58,343
Let's bring Lisbon into view.

8
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:09,069
Lisbon, called Lisboa in Portuguese, stands on the Tagus river on Portugal's
west coast, where the river meets the Atlantic.

9
00:01:09,729 --> 00:01:16,463
Probably Phoenician Alis Ubbo, "safe harbour", though the Romans preferred a
legend about Ulysses founding it.

10
00:01:17,112 --> 00:01:28,455
Remember Lisbon as the safe harbour, and the city whose 1755 earthquake led to
the first scientific study of an earthquake anywhere.

11
00:01:29,142 --> 00:01:31,522
Let's bring Athens into view.

12
00:01:34,926 --> 00:01:41,149
Athens stands in the south of Greece, in the Attic plain, close to the Saronic
Gulf.

13
00:01:41,804 --> 00:01:48,793
Named for the goddess Athena, who in the myth won the city from Poseidon with
the gift of an olive tree.

14
00:01:49,449 --> 00:01:59,085
Remember Athens as the olive tree won from Poseidon, the Parthenon above the
city, and the first modern Olympic Games in 1896.

15
00:01:59,759 --> 00:02:02,487
Let's bring Valletta into view.

16
00:02:05,393 --> 00:02:11,999
Valletta stands on a peninsula on Malta's north-east coast, in the middle of
the Mediterranean.

17
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:21,044
Named for Jean de Valette, grand master of the Knights of Saint John, who held
Malta against the Ottomans in 1565.

18
00:02:21,707 --> 00:02:30,914
Remember Valletta as the city of the grand master who held Malta in 1565, and
one of the smallest capitals in the European Union.

19
00:02:35,964 --> 00:02:46,494
Madrid and Lisbon are the two Iberian capitals, Athens the old one of the
Mediterranean, and Valletta the island capital off Sicily.

20
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:57,864
Remember the source of water, the safe harbour, the olive tree of Athena, and
the grand master who held Malta in 1565.
